WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.339
"Mayor Hubbletree didn't sound very welcoming in his 'welcome' speech," Ben whispered to Winnie.

2
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.316
"Monsters make him nervous," Winnie whispered back.

3
00:00:14.317 --> 00:00:20.461
Mr. Freaky's noses were wiggling wildly as he tried to reassure Mayor Hubbletree.

4
00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:25.763
"Don't worry, Mayor. Miss Bungle and I will make sure that things are under control."

5
00:00:25.764 --> 00:00:29.654
"You'd better, Freaky!" Mayor Hubbletree snapped.

6
00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:33.181
"I went to a lot of trouble to arrange this field trip.

7
00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:38.134
A lot of people are very suspicious of monsters, you know."

8
00:00:38.135 --> 00:00:43.073
Dr. Bones looked impatient. "Don't worry, Mayor.

9
00:00:43.074 --> 00:00:46.399
Everything will be fine.

10
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.913
I'll make sure that all the monsters are snug in their beds."

11
00:00:51.914 --> 00:00:56.681
"I have a coffin, not a bed," said a vampire.

12
00:00:56.682 --> 00:00:59.734
"I have a pyramid," Cleo said.

13
00:00:59.735 --> 00:01:07.528
Winnie giggled. "Do you think we should tell Dr. Bones that zombies never sleep?"

14
00:01:07.529 --> 00:01:11.554
"Wonderful, Dr. Bones!" the mayor was saying.

15
00:01:11.555 --> 00:01:15.676
"I look forward to receiving a wonderful report tomorrow.

16
00:01:15.677 --> 00:01:22.133
Now please excuse me. I have some very important work to do at City Hall."

17
00:01:22.134 --> 00:01:30.938
As the mayor left, the Doppel Gang made funny faces behind his back.

18
00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:36.016
"Stop that at once!" Mr. Freaky ordered.

19
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:41.735
Dr. Bones turned to Al Normal. "You're in charge," she said.

20
00:01:41.736 --> 00:01:45.737
"I'll be in my office."

21
00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:49.928
Al Normal looked nervously at the group.

22
00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:55.728
"Okay, people, er, monsters! Let's go inside."

23
00:01:55.729 --> 00:02:04.925
Ben followed the other monsters into the museum.

24
00:02:04.926 --> 00:02:10.834
"I'm sure that you'll find many interesting things here," Al Normal began.

25
00:02:10.835 --> 00:02:17.873
"We have all kinds of fascinating exhibits—dinosaurs, rocks, plants.

26
00:02:17.874 --> 00:02:26.032
We also have a wonderful Old West exhibit and an Egyptian collection with valuable jewels."

27
00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:30.707
"Ooh! Dinosaurs!" said a lizard monster.

28
00:02:30.708 --> 00:02:35.330
Gaby pointed to a fountain. "What a pretty fountain."

29
00:02:35.331 --> 00:02:40.564
"It represents the oceans of the world," Mr. Normal said.

30
00:02:40.565 --> 00:02:44.061
"There's a map of the museum right here."

31
00:02:44.062 --> 00:02:47.604
He pointed to a big map on display.

32
00:02:47.605 --> 00:02:51.023
Beside it was a stand with printed maps.

33
00:02:51.024 --> 00:02:53.983
Al Normal looked at Miss Bungle and Mr. Freaky.

34
00:02:53.984 --> 00:02:58.539
"Should I show the students around the museum?" he asked.

35
00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:03.884
"I think they can explore the exhibits on their own," Miss Bungle said.

36
00:03:03.885 --> 00:03:09.070
"I don't want anyone to get lost," Al Normal murmured.

37
00:03:09.071 --> 00:03:12.999
"No problem. We can use the maps," Ben said.

38
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.752
Al Normal still looked uneasy.

39
00:03:15.753 --> 00:03:25.111
"I'll be walking around the exhibits, watching to see if anyone needs me."

40
00:03:25.112 --> 00:03:33.296
"Too bad he doesn't have more eyes," whispered a three-eyed monster.

41
00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:37.465
"I wonder where the Egyptian exhibit is," Cleo said. "I

42
00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:42.133
bet we can find it," Waldo replied, looking at his map. "Let's

43
00:03:42.134 --> 00:03:46.472
check out the Early Humans exhibit first," Gaby suggested. "I

44
00:03:46.473 --> 00:03:49.441
read that people used to live in caves." "Wow!"

45
00:03:49.442 --> 00:03:55.964
Mog said. "Maybe they're more like monsters than I thought." Ben

46
00:03:55.965 --> 00:04:01.430
and Winnie started exploring the museum. They

47
00:04:01.431 --> 00:04:06.878
looked at the cave people and then headed to the dinosaur exhibit. A

48
00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:13.102
few monsters were standing at a glass case. "Ugh!"

49
00:04:13.103 --> 00:04:16.222
cried a fish monster. "I

50
00:04:16.223 --> 00:04:19.055
thought they'd have real dinosaurs here. These

51
00:04:19.056 --> 00:04:21.513
are just dumb skeletons!" A

52
00:04:21.514 --> 00:04:29.214
tall skeleton glowered at the fish monster. "Are you calling skeletons dumb?" Waldo

53
00:04:29.215 --> 00:04:32.582
read aloud from a museum pamphlet. "It

54
00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:38.995
says here that ancient people thought that huge fossil bones belonged to giants." "Maybe

55
00:04:38.996 --> 00:04:43.072
they did belong to giants," Gaby said. "But

56
00:04:43.073 --> 00:04:50.627
now people know those bones really belonged to dinosaurs, which are long extinct," Waldo continued. "How

57
00:04:50.628 --> 00:04:54.948
do they know dinosaurs are extinct?" asked the fish monster. "Dinosaurs

58
00:04:54.949 --> 00:04:57.899
could still be roaming the earth." While

59
00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:05.229
the others argued about the bones, Ben walked around. He

60
00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:09.837
spotted a pair of zombies standing near the museum entrance. "They

61
00:05:09.838 --> 00:05:12.825
must be new students," Ben thought. "I

62
00:05:12.826 --> 00:05:15.882
didn't notice them on the bus." He

63
00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:20.186
decided to walk over and introduce himself. But

64
00:05:20.187 --> 00:05:25.472
he lost the zombies in the crowd before he could reach them. "Huh.

65
00:05:25.473 --> 00:05:29.933
Where did they go?" he said, looking around. Nearby,

66
00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:35.668
some people in hard hats came out of the construction area. "Excuse

67
00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:43.719
me, did you see two zombies go by?" Ben asked them. "Nope,"

68
00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:50.322
said the first worker, whom Ben had seen at the director's office earlier. "Hey,"

69
00:05:50.323 --> 00:05:53.590
said another worker with a frown. "Shouldn't

70
00:05:53.591 --> 00:05:56.574
you be with the other monsters? Dr.

71
00:05:56.575 --> 00:06:01.393
Bones doesn't like students wandering around the museum on their own." "Dr.

72
00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:06.427
Bones doesn't like anybody ," the first worker muttered under his breath.

73
00:06:06.428 --> 00:06:11.115
Just then Ben heard a shriek.

74
00:06:11.116 --> 00:06:14.008
"That sounds like Cleo!" he thought.

75
00:06:14.009 --> 00:06:20.639
He thanked the workers and whirled around to see what was happening.

76
00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.350
He found his friends at the Egyptian exhibit.

77
00:06:23.351 --> 00:06:31.485
They were all staring into a tall glass display case, just past the Egyptian jewels.

78
00:06:31.486 --> 00:06:34.197
Cleo had her hands clapped over her mouth.

79
00:06:34.198 --> 00:06:37.429
"Cleo, what's wrong?" Ben asked.

80
00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.797
Cleo pointed at the case.

81
00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:47.479
"See that mummy? He's my uncle Tut!"

